          "lead_raw_text": " The structure of Ca6Ce2 (reduced formula Ca3Ce) crystallizes in the hexagonal space group P6_3/mmc (No. 194), with eight atoms per unit cell distributed over two independent Wyckoff orbits. Geometry-derived analysis shows both Ca and Ce centers adopt a close-packed-like local arrangement with 12 geometric neighbors each, at distances of 3.8217–3.9672 Å; Ca centers coordinate with 8 Ca and 4 Ce neighbors, while Ce centers coordinate with 12 Ca neighbors. The geometric neighbor graph is fully connected in three dimensions. Validated polyhedron-sharing analysis identifies 12-vertex Ca–Ca and Ca–Ce coordination polyhedra exhibiting corner, edge, and face sharing, though these relations are not exclusive to all polyhedra.\n<CRYSTAL_START>",
